53,DETAIL
54,/afk [<message>]
55,Toggles your AFK ("Away From Keyboard") state between on/off. If optional message is specified, sets you to AFK with a custom response. When AFK is on you will still receive messages, but anyone tuning or sending to you will receive an AFK notice.
56,/all <message>
57,Broadcasts a message to ALL players. Logged
58,/allied <message>
59,Broadcasts a message to all ALLIED players. Logged
60,/axis <message>
61,Broadcasts a message to all AXIS players. Logged
62,/crs [<message>]
63,Without arguments: lists staff online. With arguments: sends a message to the CRS channel.
64,/gm [<message>]
65,Without arguments: lists GMs online. With arguments: sends a message to the GM channel.
66,/gmmode
67,Toggles GM 'lurk' mode on/off
68,/grab <player> [<reason>]
69,Starts a direct conversation with <player> which limits both of you to communicating exclusively and by default with each other. Conversations are fully logged. Use /ungrab to release. Logged
70,/hc [<message>]
71,Without a message: lists people tuned to HC channel. Otherwise sends <message> to the HC channel.
72,/hc
73,Lists HC officers currently online.
74,/hcoff
75,Detunes the HC channel
76,/hcon
77,Tunes to the HC channel
78,/help [<command>]
79,Lists server commands or shows help for specified command
80,/hqoff
81,Turns off receipt of HQ messages.
82,/hqon
83,Enables receipt of HQ messages.
84,/kick <player> [<message>]
85,If player is spawned forces them to exit to desktop. Message is optional. Logged
86,/kickall <reason>
87,Forces all spawned players to exit to desktop. Logged
88,/m <player> <message>
89,Sends a private message to <player>
90,/N <message>
91,Sends <message> only on the radio tuned in the specified slot (1-6)
92,/pinfo <player>
93,Displays host information about a player
94,/report <problem>
95,Submits a brief, one-line, problem/bug/cheat/exploit/complaint to CRS. Reports are reviewed daily but may also be viewed by GMs online. Please note however that this is a reporting tool only; we do not respond individually to reports
96,/roster
97,Shows player numbers
98,/sys <message>
99,Broadcasts an anonymous SYSTEM message to all players. Logged
100,/sysmotd [<message>]
101,Sets or displays the System M.O.T.D ("Message Of The Day"). Logged
102,/sysmotd
103,Displays the current System M.O.T.D ("Message of The Day")
104,/ungrab
105,Release a previously /grab'd player. Logged
106,/warn <player> <message>
107,Sends a WARNING message to <player>. Logged
108,/warnall <message>
109,Sends a WARNING message to ALL players online. Logged
110,/who [<player1> ... <player4>]
111,without arguments: lists squad members online; with arguments: shows whether specified players are on- or off-line - for squad members it also shows where they are in-game.
112,/cpdump [detail] [<town>]
113,Shows detailed information for origin- or specified-town. Specify "detail" for full information.
114,/cpinfo [<town>]
115,Shows summary information for origin- or specified-town.
116,/own [<town>]
117,With town: Shows ownership for the specified town. Without town: Shows ownership information for the closest town.
